2920: /// Wraps a [_BlockRenderer] so that the underlying block widget (and its
2921: /// [_TextSelectionSurface] children, geometry registration, and text-layout
2922: /// cache) stay mounted even when scrolled out of the viewport — but only when
2923: /// [keepAlive] is true. Used to keep the caret block and selection endpoints
2924: /// alive under editor virtualisation, so the caret and selection
2925: /// highlight always paint and the geometry registry always knows their box.
2926: ///
2927: /// Also drives incremental rebuild: a block is only re-rendered when its
2928: /// content changed ([blockChanged]) *or* when the selection / caret / IME
2929: /// composition touches it. A pure caret move inside a different block leaves
2930: /// this block's cached child intact, avoiding the inline-span rebuild that
2931: /// would otherwise run for every block on every keystroke.
