**Refining command logic**

I need a more robust command to update the selection. If the moved block is selected with the caret at the same offset, then the block index changes. If the selection is on other blocks, the index gets adjusted. It seems that the acceptance criteria state the target of the moved block is selected. I'll ensure the existing toolbar selection for the move goes to the end of the moved block. I think tests should also consider undo/redo selection restoration. Commands create a changeset that includes selections before and after, which is good!
